WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.448
Digestion needs both mixing and forward movement.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.670
In the small intestine,
segmentation uses localized rhythmic contractions

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.460
to divide and mix chyme against the absorbing surface.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.230
Watch neighboring sections narrow
and relax while the contents

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.773
remain in the same region.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.640
Peristalsis serves a different purpose.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.093
A coordinated contraction wave
moves the contents onward.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.828
Now the narrowing travels,
and the bolus advances ahead

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.120
of it.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.557
Mixing improves contact; propulsion changes location.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.078
This distinction comes from
Chapter forty, slide forty-six.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.227
The illustrated timing and motion are schematic.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.714
The source does not
supply a complete motor-control pathway.
